From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_LANDING_TRACE=1: a log of the GPU results that land in guest memory, present by present; a diagnostic, off by default

Run a frame ahead (EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1), Ocarina's picture is about twice too bright for a
second after a cut from black in 12 of 32 door runs, and in 0 of 45 with the full wait. The
exposure is set from a wrong reading there. EDEN_UP_AHEAD_LOAD_WAIT (0511) could not catch the
cut: the game draws the whole scene under the black and no present comes late.

To find the reading: with this switch each present logs whether it returned before its frame's
fence, and each small piece of GPU-written data that lands in guest memory (buffer cache
downloads, with a mark when bytes were kept off because the guest CPU wrote there first; texture
cache buffer and image downloads) logs its address, size and first 32 bytes against the game's
latest present. At most 24 lines a present; landings over 256 bytes are only counted.

diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
index b224d69..075340e 100644
--- a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
+++ b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@
 #include "core/frontend/framebuffer_layout.h"
 #include "core/perf_stats.h"
 #include "video_core/ahead_guard.h"
+#include "video_core/landing_trace.h"
 #include "video_core/gpu.h"
 #include "video_core/gpu_split.h"
 #include "video_core/ubo_snapshot.h"
@@ -2041,10 +2042,17 @@ private:
             m_stats.pace_us += to_us(paced - composited);
             m_stats.max_fence_us = (std::max<long long>)(m_stats.max_fence_us, static_cast<long long>(to_us(waited - entered)));
             // Counted at the reply: the game gets its buffers back with this frame unfinished.
-            if (const u32 fence_id = ~w[22]; fence_id < 192 &&
-                !system.Host1x().GetSyncpointManager().IsReadyGuest(fence_id, w[24])) {
+            const bool ran_ahead_now =
+                ~w[22] < 192 &&
+                !system.Host1x().GetSyncpointManager().IsReadyGuest(~w[22], w[24]);
+            if (ran_ahead_now) {
                 ++m_stats.ran_ahead;
             }
+            // EDEN_UP_LANDING_TRACE (video_core/landing_trace.h): the downloads that land from
+            // here on are logged against this present.
+            if (VideoCommon::LandingTrace::Enabled()) [[unlikely]] {
+                VideoCommon::LandingTrace::AtPresent(m_presents, ran_ahead_now);
+            }
             // EDEN_UP_LIVE_SWITCHES=1 (common/live_switch.h): a live schedule changes its
             // switches here, between two presents, and counts this present for the phase.
             Common::LiveSwitch::AtPresent(entered);
